//ERR 15 11 15 12
//MSG="Unrecognized escape character"

// An escape the preprocessor does not recognise is rejected inside a string,
// the same way it already was inside a character literal — see
// 56e_unknown_escape_in_char.cpl. 15_string_escapes.cpl lists the ones that are
// recognised.
//
// This used to be a split between the two: the character literal rejected the
// unknown escape while the string kept the backslash verbatim, so "a\tb" was
// the four characters a \ t b and someone reaching for a tab got a backslash
// and no diagnostic. The case that recorded the old behaviour,
// 25_unrecognized_string_escape_stays_literal.cpl, is gone along with it.

fn main
    out "a\tb"
